###############################################################################################
# FHIR API - one request per endpoint (Visual Studio / VS Code REST Client)
# Start MockEhr.Api (5090) and FHIRAPI (5100) first. Explanations: ../docs/FHIRAPI-Guide.md
###############################################################################################

@fhir = http://localhost:5100/fhir/r4
@root = http://localhost:5100
# Security:InternalApiKey of the FHIR API (the Payer Gateway sends it). Needed on /internal and on /fhir/r4 without a token.
@apiKey = local-test-internal-key

### 1. CapabilityStatement (public)
GET {{fhir}}/metadata

### 2. SMART discovery (public)
GET {{fhir}}/.well-known/smart-configuration

### 3. Read one resource
GET {{fhir}}/Patient/pat-1
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

###
GET {{fhir}}/MedicationRequest/ord-1-retacrit
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Coverage by id works after the order (or a Coverage search) was read - see CoveragePatientIndex
# Coverage ids are built by the API (Helpers/CoverageIds): copy the id from a Coverage?patient= search first.
GET {{fhir}}/Coverage/cov-1
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

###
GET {{fhir}}/PractitionerRole/role-prac-1
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

###
GET {{fhir}}/DocumentReference/doc-knee-xray
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

###
GET {{fhir}}/Binary/doc-knee-xray
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 4. Search
GET {{fhir}}/Coverage?patient=pat-1&status=active
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

###
GET {{fhir}}/MedicationRequest?_id=ord-1-retacrit&_include=MedicationRequest:patient&_include=MedicationRequest:requester&_include=MedicationRequest:insurance
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

###
GET {{fhir}}/ServiceRequest?_id=ord-mri-lumbar,ord-mri-brain&_include=ServiceRequest:requester:PractitionerRole
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

###
GET {{fhir}}/Observation?patient=pat-1&code=http://loinc.org|39156-5,http://loinc.org|59408-5
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

###
GET {{fhir}}/Condition?patient=pat-1&clinical-status=active
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

###
GET {{fhir}}/DocumentReference?patient=pat-1&type=http://loinc.org|18748-4
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Missing parameter -> 400 OperationOutcome that says what to add
GET {{fhir}}/Observation
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 5. Save a DTR form with a known id (201 first time, 200 after)
PUT {{fhir}}/QuestionnaireResponse/qr-retacrit-1
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/fhir+json

{
  "resourceType": "QuestionnaireResponse",
  "id": "qr-retacrit-1",
  "meta": { "profile": [ "http://hl7.org/fhir/us/davinci-dtr/StructureDefinition/dtr-questionnaireresponse" ] },
  "extension": [
    { "url": "http://hl7.org/fhir/us/davinci-dtr/StructureDefinition/qr-context", "valueReference": { "reference": "MedicationRequest/ord-1-retacrit" } },
    { "url": "http://hl7.org/fhir/us/davinci-dtr/StructureDefinition/qr-context", "valueReference": { "reference": "Coverage/cov-1" } }
  ],
  "questionnaire": "http://example.org/fhir/Questionnaire/retacrit-esa",
  "status": "completed",
  "subject": { "reference": "Patient/pat-1" },
  "authored": "2026-10-01T11:00:00Z",
  "author": { "reference": "Practitioner/prac-1" },
  "item": [
    { "linkId": "hemoglobin-lab", "item": [
      { "linkId": "hemoglobin-date", "answer": [ { "valueDate": "2026-09-20" } ] },
      { "linkId": "hemoglobin", "answer": [ { "valueDecimal": 9.4,
        "extension": [ { "url": "http://hl7.org/fhir/us/davinci-dtr/StructureDefinition/information-origin",
                         "extension": [ { "url": "source", "valueCode": "auto" } ] } ] } ] }
    ] },
    { "linkId": "face-to-face", "answer": [ { "valueBoolean": true } ] },
    { "linkId": "attestation", "answer": [ { "valueBoolean": true } ] }
  ]
}

### 6. Create a DTR form, server assigns the id (201 + Location)
POST {{fhir}}/QuestionnaireResponse
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/fhir+json

{
  "resourceType": "QuestionnaireResponse",
  "questionnaire": "http://example.org/fhir/Questionnaire/retacrit-esa",
  "status": "in-progress",
  "subject": { "reference": "Patient/pat-1" },
  "item": [ { "linkId": "face-to-face", "answer": [ { "valueBoolean": true } ] } ]
}

### 7. Read a form / all forms of a patient
GET {{fhir}}/QuestionnaireResponse/qr-retacrit-1
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

###
GET {{fhir}}/QuestionnaireResponse?patient=pat-1
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### What the EHR received (mock EHR)
GET http://localhost:5090/api/patients/pat-1/questionnaire-responses
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}


###############################################################################################
# Payer Gateway and Keycloak calls (/internal)
###############################################################################################

### 8. SMART launch for the DTR app (the gateway creates it when the clinician opens the DTR link)
# @name launch
POST {{root}}/internal/smart-launches
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": "pat-1",
  "insurancePlanId": 1001,
  "userPractitionerId": "prac-1",
  "encounterId": "enc-1",
  "fhirContext": [ "MedicationRequest/ord-1-retacrit", "Coverage/cov-1" ],
  "appContext": "{\"questionnaire\":[\"http://example.org/fhir/Questionnaire/retacrit-esa\"]}"
}

### 9. Keycloak only: the launch context, as the Keycloak SMART launch add-on reads it (client of payer 1001)
GET {{root}}/internal/smart-launches/{{launch.response.body.launchId}}/context?clientId=mock-payer-dtr-app&insurancePlanId=1001
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 9b. The same launch for another payer's client -> 403
GET {{root}}/internal/smart-launches/{{launch.response.body.launchId}}/context?clientId=other-app&insurancePlanId=2002
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 10. SMART discovery: the app finds Keycloak's endpoints here
GET {{fhir}}/.well-known/smart-configuration


###############################################################################################
# Security:TokenProvider = "BuiltIn" (default): this API issues the tokens.
# The mock EHR's test app "mock-payer-dtr-app" (PA_SMART_CLIENT, payer 1001, redirect http://localhost:5300/callback)
# and the RFC 7636 PKCE example pair:
#   code_verifier  dBjftJeZ4CVP-mB92K27uhbUJU1p1r_wW1gFWFOEjXk
#   code_challenge E9Melhoa2OwvFrEMTJguCHaoeK1t8URWbuGJSstw-cM   (S256)
# Run 8 (launch) first.
###############################################################################################

### B1. fhirAuthorization token for a payer (the gateway sends it in the CRD hook call)
POST {{root}}/internal/access-tokens
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "subject": "MOCK-DAVINCI", "patientId": "pat-1", "minutes": 5 }

### B2. Authorize -> 302; copy "code" from the Location header into @builtInCode below
# @no-redirect
GET {{fhir}}/auth/authorize?response_type=code&client_id=mock-payer-dtr-app&redirect_uri=http://localhost:5300/callback&launch={{launch.response.body.launchId}}&scope=launch%20fhirUser%20patient/*.rs%20patient/QuestionnaireResponse.cu&state=abc123&aud={{fhir}}&code_challenge=E9Melhoa2OwvFrEMTJguCHaoeK1t8URWbuGJSstw-cM&code_challenge_method=S256

###
@builtInCode = paste-code-here

### B3. Token: code -> access token + patient, encounter, fhirUser, fhirContext, appContext
# @name builtInToken
POST {{fhir}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code&code={{builtInCode}}&redirect_uri=http://localhost:5300/callback&client_id=mock-payer-dtr-app&code_verifier=dBjftJeZ4CVP-mB92K27uhbUJU1p1r_wW1gFWFOEjXk

### B4. The app reads its patient with the BuiltIn token -> 200
GET {{fhir}}/Patient/pat-1
Authorization: Bearer {{builtInToken.response.body.access_token}}


###############################################################################################
# Security:TokenProvider = "Keycloak": SMART EHR launch as a payer DTR app does it - sign-in and tokens at Keycloak.
# TODO: http://localhost:8080/realms/ehr is a local test realm; use the realm of Keycloak:Authority.
# 11. Open this address in a browser (Keycloak signs you in through Azure AD), then copy "code" from the address the
#     browser is sent to (http://localhost:5300/callback?code=...) into @code below:
#   http://localhost:8080/realms/ehr/protocol/openid-connect/auth?response_type=code&client_id=mock-payer-dtr-app&redirect_uri=http://localhost:5300/callback&launch=LAUNCH_ID&scope=openid%20launch%20fhirUser%20patient/*.rs%20patient/QuestionnaireResponse.cu&state=abc123&aud=http://localhost:5100/fhir/r4&code_challenge=E9Melhoa2OwvFrEMTJguCHaoeK1t8URWbuGJSstw-cM&code_challenge_method=S256
# PKCE pair (RFC 7636 example): code_verifier dBjftJeZ4CVP-mB92K27uhbUJU1p1r_wW1gFWFOEjXk
###############################################################################################
@keycloak = http://localhost:8080/realms/ehr
@code = paste-code-here

### 11b. Token at Keycloak: code -> access token + patient, encounter, fhirUser, fhirContext, appContext
# @name token
POST {{keycloak}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code&code={{code}}&redirect_uri=http://localhost:5300/callback&client_id=mock-payer-dtr-app&code_verifier=dBjftJeZ4CVP-mB92K27uhbUJU1p1r_wW1gFWFOEjXk

### 12. The app reads its patient with the token -> 200
GET {{fhir}}/Patient/pat-1
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}

### 13. Another patient with the same token -> 403 (forbidden)
GET {{fhir}}/Patient/pat-2
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}

### 14. No token, no key -> 401
GET {{fhir}}/Patient/pat-1
